# torque.obdtrace v1
# vehicle: 2015 Mazda 3 2.0 petrol
# adapter: OBDLink MX+
# protocol: 6 (ISO 15765-4 CAN 11/500)
# notes: The SPEC 5.4 scan end to end, on a stopped car with the engine
# notes: idling: stored P0301 + P0420, pending P0133, permanent P0420,
# notes: MIL on and 3 codes claimed. Headers ON, as ATH1 really produces.
# notes: Then Mode 04 is accepted and the re-read comes back with the
# notes: stored and pending lists empty and the PERMANENT code still
# notes: there — which is what permanent means, and must not be reported
# notes: as "the code came straight back".
# notes: Mode 02 answers with the freeze frame the ECU kept for P0301 — an idle misfire, engine still warming;
# notes: its Mode 02 masks match its Mode 01 ones, so fuel (2F) and module voltage (42) are in the frame too.
